{"availability":"available","full":"fedepaj/solargaze","name":"solargaze","description":"Open-source sun and shadow simulator on Google's photorealistic 3D tiles. No build step.","category":"Other","language":"Python","stars":0,"forks":0,"created":"2026-09-20T22:05:27Z","updated":"2026-10-09T12:20:25Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"fedepaj.github.io/solargaze","topics":[],"demo":"https://fedepaj.github.io/solargaze/","color":"#63362a","ink":"#f8c7a8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-09T13:18:34.519Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-09T13:18:34.519Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-09T13:18:34.519Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-04T06:50:58.085Z","stars":0,"forks":0},{"at":"2026-10-05T05:50:35.837Z","stars":0,"forks":0},{"at":"2026-10-07T11:14:47.720Z","stars":0,"forks":0},{"at":"2026-10-09T13:18:34.519Z","stars":0,"forks":0}],"technologies":["Python"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Go anywhere — a square, a village, a vineyard, a valley, a mountain ridge — and see what it is like to stand there. Drag two sliders, time of day and day of year, and real shadows move across the same 3D world Google Earth draws; switch on a layer and the ground shows which surfaces bake on a clear morning and stay warm on a clear night, how the air sits street by street, how the wind threads between the buildings. Hour by hour, season by season. No build step, no server: a folder of static files that runs on GitHub Pages.","Sunrise to sunset over the Colosseum — try it live. The ring is a compass card lying on the ground, the glowing arc is the sun's track for that day, and the beam arrives from the sun's direction into the studied point."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/fedepaj/solargaze/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"e794f8ea0f82b4ad17199cfa25cd030cf715327fd6d91943150dc540fe7a95e7","extractedAt":"2026-10-09T23:12:54.373Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-09T23:12:54.373Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"Go anywhere — a square, a villa